@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About — Apex Coaching</PageTitle>

<section class="page-head">
    <h1>About Apex Coaching</h1>
</section>

<section class="about">
    <div class="about-text">
        <p>
            Apex Coaching connects people with independent personal trainers and gives both sides
            the tools to run the relationship — programming, scheduling, progress tracking, and
            billing — in one place.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>For clients</strong>, that means browsing verified trainers, buying a package
            that fits, booking sessions, and following a program built for you, with billing handled
            in the same portal.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>For trainers</strong>, it means a profile that markets itself, package and
            pricing control, a client roster with lead tracking, and payouts that arrive without
            chasing invoices.
        </p>
        <p>
            The platform takes a commission on each transaction; trainers keep the rest and stay
            independent.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="about-note">
    <p>
        <em>
            This is a demonstration build. Trainers, clients, bookings, and payments shown in the
            portals are seeded sample data, and checkout runs in simulated mode unless live payment
            keys are configured.
        </em>
    </p>
</section>
